{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DECISIVE RESULT: THE JOB FAILS ON MAIN ITSELF. The manually dispatched run 33839813271 (test.yml against main, branch-head lane) reports:\n  scanner-integration / pinned Semgrep + Gitleaks contracts -> FAILURE\n\nSo this is NOT a property of 'changes trying to land'. On main the tree contains\nscripts/install_review_scanners.py and the workflow's own commit, and the job STILL FAILS. Main is\nred on this gate right now, independently of anything in review.\n\nTHAT SETTLES THE CAUTION I RAISED ABOVE AND CONFIRMS TWO DISTINCT FAILURES ARE IN PLAY:\n - Change 2600 (base 08a39c39c50d, PREDATES the file) failed with\n   'python: can't open file .../scripts/install_review_scanners.py: [Errno 2] No such file or\n   directory' -- a genuine predates-the-gate miss, and the guard that should have caught it\n   (GUARDED_WORKFLOWS in tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py) does not list\n   _scanner-integration.yml.\n - Main, and change 2607 (branched FROM 6125c5345f01), both HAVE the file and fail anyway. So there\n   is a second, independent fault in the job itself.\nFixing only the guard-list omission would therefore leave main red. Both need addressing.\n\nI could not retrieve the main run's log tail while the run was still in progress -- worth pulling\nonce it completes (job id 100919632441, run 33839813271), since that log is from a tree with every\nprerequisite present and so isolates the second fault cleanly, exactly as change 2608 isolated the\njob from change content.\n\nRecording the operator's reasoning that got here, because it is the better diagnostic move and I did\nnot make it unprompted: check whether the branch-head lane is failing on main FIRST. If main is\ngreen, the fault is in what is landing; if main is red, the fault is in the thing itself. I had gone\nstraight to per-change comparison without ever establishing the base rate.\n\nStill not working this ticket -- handing on to the owning session."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788499960545842001,"uuid":"f230d67b-91ce-4328-acff-6a1a34f3957c"}